17d3|a|Disordered in intellect; crazy; insane. ; Excited beyond self-control or the restraint of reason; inflamed by violent or uncontrollable desire, passion, or appetite; as, to be mad with terror, lust, or hatred; mad against political reform. ; Proceeding from, or indicating, madness; expressing distraction; prompted by infatuation, fury, or extreme rashness. ; Extravagant; immoderate. ; Furious with rage, terror, or disease; -- said of the lower animals; as, a mad bull; esp., having hydrophobia; rabid; as, a mad dog. ; Angry; out of patience; vexed; as, to get mad at a person. ; Having impaired polarity; -- applied to a compass needle.	j:1re9,79,5;17d3,70,5;1skd,64,9;lqv,63,5;gb1,61,2;1m64,59,2;uih,54,3;13ja,49,5;1px0,48,2;17eu,46,1;rlq,45,2;hsn,45,6;18vi,41,1;17s5,18,3~1skd,64,9;hsn,45,6;1re9,79,5;17d3,70,5;13ja,49,5;lqv,63,5;17s5,18,3;uih,54,3;rlq,45,2;1px0,48,2;1m64,59,2;gb1,61,2;17eu,46,1;18vi,41,1	e:1vcq,21,4;e9a,10,4;1lgp,9,5;1np9,1,3~1lgp,9,5;e9a,10,4;1vcq,21,4;1np9,1,3
