17z6|v|To cover or envelop, as with a mantle; to cloak; to hide; to disguise. ; To unfold and spread out the wings, like a mantle; -- said of hawks. Also used figuratively. ; To spread out; -- said of wings. ; To spread over the surface as a covering; to overspread; as, the scum mantled on the pool. ; To gather, assume, or take on, a covering, as froth, scum, etc.	s:mss,37,1~mss,37,1
