1822|n|The third month of the year, containing thirty-one days. ; A territorial border or frontier; a region adjacent to a boundary line; a confine; -- used chiefly in the plural, and in English history applied especially to the border land on the frontiers between England and Scotland, and England and Wales. ; The act of marching; a movement of soldiers from one stopping place to another; military progress; advance of troops. ; Hence: Measured and regular advance or movement, like that of soldiers moving in order; stately or deliberate walk; steady onward movement. ; The distance passed over in marching; as, an hour's march; a march of twenty miles. ; A piece of music designed or fitted to accompany and guide the movement of troops; a piece of music in the march form.	a:101g,76,4;19ip,38,3;15bt,37,7;22bs,35,4;n3o,31,4;1gr1,23,4;ms7,22,3;1ad0,14,1;1as8,10,1;1ces,6,5;15bd,3,6~15bt,37,7;15bd,3,6;1ces,6,5;22bs,35,4;101g,76,4;1gr1,23,4;n3o,31,4;19ip,38,3;ms7,22,3;1as8,10,1;1ad0,14,1	v:htg,73,9;1q5g,69,3;6wq,51,7;1p91,36,4;1ad0,29,3;1kj1,25,3;19ip,22,1;1xim,16,5;1mo9,14,2~htg,73,9;6wq,51,7;1xim,16,5;1p91,36,4;1kj1,25,3;1ad0,29,3;1q5g,69,3;1mo9,14,2;19ip,22,1	V:p4s,56,2;18oi,43,4;s80,35,1;dz1,8,3~18oi,43,4;dz1,8,3;p4s,56,2;s80,35,1	n:1mbm,96,5;r9u,60,2;2278,59,1;tco,56,2;1s59,55,1;1zcv,51,1;hx6,44,5;1as8,20,2;29mh,15,1;22bs,15,1;huw,13,4;261u,9,6;1utw,8,11;htf,8,2;29ke,7,3~1utw,8,11;7fd,2,8;261u,9,6;hx6,44,5;4m6,3,5;1mbm,96,5;huw,13,4;29ke,7,3;r9u,60,2;htf,8,2;tco,56,2;1as8,20,2;1zcv,51,1;29mh,15,1;22bs,15,1	N:4yp,85,4;p4s,80,10;y1s,79,3;46m,41,2;18oi,39,3;s80,35,1;n1u,35,3;1t56,17,5;1p90,1,2~p4s,80,10;1t56,17,5;4yp,85,4;y1s,79,3;n1u,35,3;18oi,39,3;46m,41,2;1p90,1,2;s80,35,1
