18aj|v|To become the master of; to subject to one's will, control, or authority; to conquer; to overpower; to subdue. ; To gain the command of, so as to understand or apply; to become an adept in; as, to master a science. ; To own; to posses. ; To be skillful; to excel.	o:21wc,9,2;1rm8,5,1;15cj,2,4;1t6k,2,1~15cj,2,4;21wc,9,2;1t6k,2,1;1rm8,5,1	s:13q8,17,2~13q8,17,2
